    '*   **Studio Sound Enhancement:** Acts as an audio enhancer, balancing voice levels and removing echo or distortion for studio-quality output.\n' +
    '*   **Multitrack Editing:** Allows simultaneous editing and syncing of multiple audio tracks (e.g., separate guest recordings) into a single podcast.\n' +
    '*   **Transcription & Summary:** Generates accurate transcripts and concise podcast summaries, complete with chapter markers and social media content.\n' +
    '*   **Batch Processing:** Supports uploading and processing multiple podcast episodes at once.\n' +
    '*   **API for Developers:** Offers an API for integrating audio/video editing and enhancement capabilities into third-party applications or workflows.\n' +
    '*   **Timeline Export:** Exports timestamps or markers of edited parts for further customization in external editors like Audacity or Audition.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Use Cases\n' +
    '\n' +
    '*   **Podcast Editing:** The primary use case. Quickly clean up episodes for a professional sound.\n' +
    '*   **Voiceover & Audiobook Production:** Enhance recordings made outside a professional studio.\n' +
    '*   **Zoom/Interview Cleaning:** Remove echo, reverb, and background noise from remote call recordings.\n' +
    '*   **Video Podcast Editing:** Clean audio from video podcasts while keeping tracks in sync (using mute edits instead of removal).\n' +
    '*   **Content Repurposing:** Use transcription and summary features to generate show notes and promotional material.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Target Users\n' +
    '\n' +
    '*   **Podcasters & Content Creators:** Individuals looking to save time and achieve professional audio without editing expertise.\n' +
    '*   **Media Agencies & Businesses:** Teams managing multiple audio/video productions.\n' +
    '*   **Audio Engineers & Editors:** Professionals using it for rough cuts or automating tedious tasks.\n' +
