fetchItem, url: https://www.essaygrader.ai mergedData: {
  link: 'https://www.essaygrader.ai',
  name: 'essaygrader',
  description: 'EssayGrader is an AI-powered, rubric-based essay grading tool for teachers that saves time and provides detailed student feedback.',
  introduction: '## Overview\n' +
    '\n' +
    'EssayGrader is a purpose-built AI essay grading platform designed for teachers and schools. It leverages artificial intelligence to grade student writing assignments against customizable rubrics and educational standards, aiming to reduce grading time while delivering consistent, detailed feedback.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Key Features & Capabilities\n' +
    '\n' +
    '- **Rubric-Based AI Grading:** Provides scores and feedback aligned to over 800 pre-built rubrics or custom rubrics uploaded by the teacher. It supports all 50 U.S. states, AP, Common Core, IB, and international standards like Cambridge and GCSE.\n' +
    '- **Standards Alignment:** Grades essays not only against the provided rubric but also measures student writing proficiency against specific state and national curriculum standards.\n' +
    '- **Pedagogical Feedback:** Generates color-coded, actionable feedback based on the Hattie & Timperley feedback model. Feedback is designed to guide student revision without providing direct answers.\n' +
    '- **Handwriting Recognition:** Can scan and grade handwritten essays from PDFs, recognizing cursive, print, and messy handwriting.\n' +
    '- **AI Content & Plagiarism Detection:** Includes built-in tools to identify AI-generated content and check for plagiarism against the web and other student submissions.\n' +
    '- **LMS Integration:** Natively integrates with Google Classroom, Canvas LMS, and Schoology, allowing teachers to import assignments and sync graded feedback and scores back directly.\n' +
    "- **Bulk Upload & Performance Insights:** Enables uploading an entire class's essays at once and provides dashboard analytics to track class-wide and individual student writing trends over time.\n" +
    '- **Multi-Language Support:** Supports grading and feedback in multiple languages, including different versions of English (U.S., U.K., Australian).\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Target Users & Use Cases\n' +
    '\n' +
    '- **Teachers (K-12 & Higher Ed):** Ideal for ELA, humanities, and social studies teachers who grade large volumes of essays, research papers, short answers, and other writing-intensive assignments. It helps combat grading fatigue and enables faster feedback cycles for student revision.\n' +
    '- **Schools & Districts:** Offers school and district-wide licenses, providing a scalable solution for consistent writing assessment across multiple classrooms.\n' +
    '- **Use Cases:** Grade narrative, argumentative, expository, analytical essays, DBQs, and more. Useful for formative assessment, providing draft feedback, and preparing students for standardized writing tests.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Unique Selling Points\n' +
    '\n' +
    '- **Teacher-Centric Design:** Built by a team that includes educators, focusing on practical workflow integration rather than just AI novelty.\n' +
    '- **Accuracy:** Benchmarked against a large dataset of teacher-graded essays, with high accuracy reported in matching or being within one point of teacher scores.\n' +
    '- **Privacy & Security:** Adheres to a privacy-first model (FERPA, COPPA compliant) where student data is not used for AI training and ownership remains with the teacher/school.',
  categories: [ 'Writing Tools', 'AI Tools', 'Office Tools' ],
  tags: [ 'AI', 'Writing', 'Automation', 'Productivity', 'Education' ],
  image: 'https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66d4ca8898912b9b735e0bb6/6984dc6a46ab420d885dec3b_EssayGrader-main.png',
