  description: 'A natural language interface for Linux commands, translating plain English into terminal instructions.',
  introduction: '## heycli - Your AI-Powered Copilot for Linux Commands\n' +
    '\n' +
    'heycli is a developer tool designed to simplify working in the Linux terminal. It acts as a natural language interpreter, allowing users to describe tasks in plain English (e.g., "hey list all files larger than 100MB") and receive the corresponding command-line syntax.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '### Key Features\n' +
    '\n' +
    '*   **Natural Language to Command Translation:** Convert everyday English descriptions into precise Linux commands.\n' +
    '*   **Terminal Integration:** Operates directly within your existing terminal workflow, requiring no shift to a separate interface.\n' +
    '*   **Learning Aid:** Helps users remember or discover command syntax, reducing the need to constantly search for documentation.\n' +
    "*   **Open Source Foundation:** The tool's client is available on GitHub, fostering transparency and community contribution.\n" +
    '\n' +
    '### Target Users & Use Cases\n' +
    '\n' +
    '*   **New Linux Users:** Ideal for those learning the command line, removing the initial barrier to entry.\n' +
    '*   **Experienced Developers:** Useful for quickly recalling seldom-used commands or translating complex logic without memorization.\n' +
    '*   **System Administrators:** Accelerates routine tasks and scripting by allowing rapid command drafting in natural language.\n' +
    '*   **Education:** Serves as an educational tool in courses teaching Linux or command-line basics.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '### Unique Selling Points\n' +
    '\n' +
    'heycli differentiates itself by focusing specifically on the command-line environment with a simple, task-oriented interface (the "hey" prefix). Its preview version is currently accessible via its GitHub repository, positioning it as a community-driven project in active development.',
  categories: [ 'Developer Tools' ],
  tags: [ 'Open Source', 'Coding', 'Productivity', 'Tech' ],
